{
  "_comment": [
    "Registers lpsd as a principal source authd will accept.",
    "",
    "The existence of the Sources\\lpsd key IS the permission. authd derives the",
    "service SID for each configured name and requires a connecting peer's token",
    "to carry it, so this key says 'a service named lpsd may assert identity on",
    "this machine' and nothing else can say it. Deleting this key stops lpsd",
    "registering; there is no second list anywhere.",
    "",
    "MayAssertForeignMemberships lifts the rule that a source may only assert",
    "groups in the same domain as the principal it just authenticated. lpsd needs",
    "it because local group membership of ANY principal is a local decision --",
    "'CORP\\Domain Admins is in BUILTIN\\Administrators' is a record this machine",
    "keeps, not something a domain controller asserts at it. A directory-backed",
    "source must NOT have this, which is what stops it declaring its own users",
    "administrators here.",
    "",
    "UnixIDBase and UnixIDCount give lpsd the range its POSIX ids land in. A",
    "source counts from 1 and knows nothing about where its range begins; authd",
    "adds the base, so lpsd's first principal (1) projects to uid 1000001.",
    "",
    "This is a containment boundary, not bookkeeping. Because the numbers a",
    "source sends are relative, the base and the count are together what stop it",
    "reaching uid 0 -- authd reserves everything below 1000000 for its own",
    "table, which begins with SYSTEM at 0 -- and what stop it reaching another",
    "source's numbers, since a relative id at or past the count is refused",
    "rather than wrapped. It is the numeric counterpart of confining a source to",
    "its domain SID.",
    "",
    "A directory source gets a base of its own, well clear of this one:",
    "10000000, say. Nothing here has to change when it arrives, which is the",
    "point of the source never knowing its own base.",
    "",
    "Absent, lpsd still authenticates but every principal projects to uid 65534",
    "(nobody). That is the safe direction -- 65534 grants nothing -- and it is",
    "visible in both the warning authd logs at registration and the uid itself.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the lpsd package into /usr/share/regim/; it only",
    "applies if an image opts in via [registry] autoapply in its peiso.toml.",
    "The package proposes, the image decides."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\Software" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Software\\Authd" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Software\\Authd\\Sources" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Software\\Authd\\Sources\\lpsd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "MayAssertForeignMemberships", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "UnixIDBase", "type": "dword", "data": 1000000 },
        { "name": "UnixIDCount", "type": "dword", "data": 1000000 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
